---
id: journey_distress_signal
title: Distress Beacon
tags: [danger, opportunity, moral]
context: journey
weight: 10
cooldown: 4
---

=== intro

A distress beacon cuts through the static—automated, cycling, desperate. The signal is weak, intermittent. Could be genuine. Could be a pirate lure. The void is full of both.

Responding would take time and fuel. Ignoring it would be easier.

* [Respond to the distress call]
  ~ fuel -= 3
  -> survivor

* [Log it and continue]
  ~ morale -= 5
  ~ chronicle "Beacon Ignored"
    We logged a distress signal but did not respond. The void is full of ghosts. We can't save them all.
  -> END

=== survivor

You find a small transport, dead in space. Power failed. Life support offline. One survivor in a pressure suit, barely conscious, air running out.

They have nothing to offer but gratitude. Their ship is scrap. Their cargo, vented. Just a person, alone in the dark, waiting to die.

* [Take them aboard]
  ~ supplies -= 3
  ~ morale += 12
  ~ addCard crew_stowaway
  ~ chronicle "Rescue"
    Pulled a survivor from the void. Another soul for the hold. They owe us their life—that's worth more than cargo.
  -> END

* [Give them supplies and coordinates to the nearest port]
  ~ supplies -= 8
  ~ chronicle "What Help We Could"
    We gave what we could spare. Patched their suit, pointed them toward salvation. Whether it was enough, we may never know.
  -> END
